WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-US

00:00:00.383 --> 00:00:03.050
(gentle music)

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:09.870
- Hey guys, Holly Wood,
product manager at ColDesi.

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.310
Today I'm gonna show you a method

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:14.550
on how to print on Mylar
bags, the black kind,

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:19.380
and we will be using our Forever
Laser Dark Transfer Paper.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:21.060
Let's get started.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.300
I am using my 9541 to print these,

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:25.620
but this process can be done

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.290
with any of our DigitalHeat FX printers.

00:00:28.290 --> 00:00:31.770
My first step was loading my
designs into print optimizer

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:32.700
and as you can see,

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:35.223
I was able to fit three designs per sheet.

00:00:37.170 --> 00:00:39.450
My next step is to take
it over to my heat press

00:00:39.450 --> 00:00:40.620
to marry the paper

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.480
and this is the process that puts the glue

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.980
on the back of the toner.

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.860
I'm using 310 for 120 seconds,

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:48.810
but always pay attention to the directions

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:52.200
that come in the box as they
can sometimes change or vary.

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.880
When the time has completed,

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:57.270
you'll want to peel immediately
in a slow fluid motion,

00:00:57.270 --> 00:00:59.490
keeping your hand as low as possible

00:00:59.490 --> 00:01:01.260
and the paper on the platen.

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:04.110
Your press will need to be
dropped to 200 for application,

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:06.450
so make sure you marry
all of your paper first

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:09.543
and plan a little break
while the press cools.

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:13.143
Now you're ready to be
trimmed and applied.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.790
Once trimmed, you can put
as many on the platinum

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:21.090
that will fit, cover with parchment paper,

00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:23.733
and is a quick ten second press.

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:30.330
Let your bags cool completely

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:32.430
and you can just roll the transfers off.

00:01:32.430 --> 00:01:34.200
I chose not to do a finishing press

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:35.820
because I like the glossy look,

00:01:35.820 --> 00:01:37.740
but if you would like
more of a matte finish,

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:39.600
you can put back into the press

00:01:39.600 --> 00:01:42.183
and cover with parchment
for five to ten seconds.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.880
So check out these finished products

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:46.230
and how beautiful they are.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:50.460
If you would like more decorating
methods for Mylar bags,

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.200
please check out the description.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.190
Thank you for joining.

00:01:53.190 --> 00:01:54.758
Until next time.

00:01:54.758 --> 00:01:58.258
(gentle music continues)

